<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">mutations</ansi>

The Chrysalis — a plague that swept across Gaius — does not merely sicken. Over time, it
reshapes those it infects. Through sustained combat, your body is pushed beyond its limits
and the Chrysalis seizes the opportunity to rewrite you.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Acquiring Mutations ━━━</ansi>

Mutations emerge on their own — you cannot choose or train for them. Each combat round you
spend in active battle builds internal pressure. When that pressure reaches a threshold, the
Chrysalis forces a change. You will see a message:

  <ansi fg="magenta">Something stirs beneath your skin. A mutation emerges: <ansi fg="yellow">Tough Skin</ansi>.</ansi>

Each subsequent mutation requires significantly more combat to trigger. Rarer mutations
contribute more weight, making the next one even harder to earn. You can carry up to five
mutations at once.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Anatomy and Mutation Compatibility ━━━</ansi>

Not every mutation is available to every creature. A mutation may require certain anatomy —
extra arms need arms to grow from, sharp claws need hands to grow on, keen eyes need eyes to
sharpen. If your species lacks the necessary body part, the mutation cannot take hold.

Conversely, some species have intrinsic mutations — natural anatomy that grants the
mechanical effect of a mutation without needing to roll for it. A wolf has an intrinsic
tail; a vampire has intrinsic regenerative tissue. Acquired mutations stack additively on
top of intrinsic ones.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Pros and Cons ━━━</ansi>

Every mutation has both benefits and drawbacks. The Chrysalis does not improve you cleanly —
it trades one capability for another. Some mutations conflict with each other and cannot
coexist in the same body.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Active Abilities ━━━</ansi>

Some mutations grant active abilities you can use in combat. These appear as commands you
can type during a fight. Active abilities share the special-move cooldown slot.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Commands ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">mutations</ansi>           List your current mutations with descriptions.
  <ansi fg="command">status</ansi>              Shows active mutations (IDs and level) in your stat panel.

